
==========================
 * From theorem premises:
A B C D E F : Points
AB = BD [00]
DA = AB [01]
CE = CA [02]
AE = AC [03]
CE ∥ DF [04]
CF ∥ ED [05]

 * Auxiliary Constructions:
: Points


 * Proof steps:
001. DF ∥ CE [04] & CF ∥ DE [05] ⇒  ∠DFC = ∠CED [06]
002. CF ∥ DE [05] ⇒  ∠DCF = ∠CDE [07]
003. ∠DFC = ∠CED [06] & ∠DCF = ∠CDE [07] (Similar Triangles)⇒  CF = DE [08]
004. ∠DFC = ∠CED [06] & ∠DCF = ∠CDE [07] (Similar Triangles)⇒  DF = CE [09]
005. AB = BD [00] & DA = AB [01] ⇒  DA = DB [10]
006. AB = AD [01] & CE = CA [02] ⇒  AB:AD = CE:CA [11]
007. AB = AD [01] & CE = CA [02] ⇒  AB:AD = CA:CE [12]
008. DB = DA [10] & AE = AC [03] ⇒  DB:DA = AE:AC [13]
009. AB:AD = CE:CA [11] & DB:DA = AE:AC [13] (Similar Triangles)⇒  BA:BD = EC:EA [14]
010. DF = CE [09] & BA:BD = EC:EA [14] & AB = BD [00] ⇒  AE = DF [15]
011. DB = DA [10] & BA:BD = EC:EA [14] & AB = BD [00] ⇒  DB:DA = EA:EC [16]
012. AB:AD = CA:CE [12] & DB:DA = EA:EC [16] (Similar Triangles)⇒  ∠(BD-CE) = ∠DAE [17]
013. ∠(BD-CE) = ∠DAE [17] & CE ∥ DF [04] ⇒  ∠BDF = ∠DAE [18]
014. DA = DB [10] & AE = DF [15] & ∠BDF = ∠DAE [18] (SAS)⇒  ED = FB [19]
015. CF = DE [08] & ED = FB [19] ⇒  BF = FC
